@startuml Topic3_Agentic_Loop
' ============================================================
' TOPIC 3: The Agentic Loop (the engine)
' Feedback LOOP, not a pipeline. 4 stages. Tool lifecycle
' is NESTED inside the ACTION + OBSERVATION stages.
' ============================================================
title Topic 3 — The Agentic Loop\n(FEEDBACK LOOP, not a pipeline — enables adaptation)

skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam roundcorner 12

start

:Task begins;

repeat
  #LightCyan:**1. PERCEPTION**\ntake in current state\n(request + full context so far);
  #LightCyan:**2. REASONING**\nthink about what to do next\n(decide the next move);
  #Orange:**3. ACTION**\nusually a TOOL CALL\n(<- tool_use block from Topic 2);
  note right
    The single tool-use ROUNDTRIP
    from Topic 2 lives INSIDE the
    Action + Observation stages.
    One heartbeat of the loop.
  end note
  #Orange:**4. OBSERVATION**\nresult comes back\n(<- tool_result block from Topic 2);
  :Append action + observation + reasoning\nto the **CONTEXT WINDOW**\n(ephemeral working memory — see note below);
repeat while (Task NOT done?) is (loop back — feed result into next PERCEPTION)
->done;

stop

floating note left
  == CONTEXT WINDOW = WORKING MEMORY ==
  * Fills up every turn (calls, results, reasoning)
  * Agent's scratchpad for THIS task
  * EPHEMERAL: vanishes at session end
    unless deliberately persisted
  * FINITE: fills up on long tasks (problem for later domain)
  ....
  == FEEDBACK LOOP vs PIPELINE ==
  * Pipeline = runs start->finish ONCE, straight line (= a workflow)
  * Loop = comes BACK around; each observation informs next decision
  * That circularity is what lets the agent ADAPT
    (recover from a failed tool, react to a surprising result)
end note

@enduml
